# The raw source files are DATA, not text, and git must not touch a byte of them.
#
# resorts.csv is cp1252-encoded — that was not a guess, it was established empirically
# (PROFILE.md §2: byte 0x96 is an en-dash, and latin-1 silently mangles 156 resort names).
# A file whose exact bytes carry a documented finding is the last file that should be
# passing through git's line-ending normalisation, which is what produced a phantom
# "500 insertions, 500 deletions" diff on a file nobody had edited.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion entirely: what is committed is what is on disk.
data/raw/** -text
*.csv -text

# Notebooks and pickles: binary, never merge them.
*.joblib binary
*.duckdb binary
